---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { profile, skills, languages, certifications, awards } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${profile.name} — ${profile.summary}`}>
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="About"
      title="Hi, I'm Polad."
      lead="I build systems that find the right document — usually in a language the big models were never really trained on."
    />

    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <p>
        I grew up in Baku and studied Computer Science at the <strong>French-Azerbaijani University
        (UFAZ)</strong>, a dual-degree programme with the University of Strasbourg and Azerbaijan
        State Oil and Industry University. I finished with a GPA of 98/100 — but the part that
        actually shaped me was starting work before I graduated.
      </p>

      <p>
        In June 2023 I joined Azerbaijan's <strong>National AI Center</strong> as an intern. I stayed
        almost three years and left as a Middle AI Engineer. Most of that time went into <a
          href="https://eqanun.ai"
          rel="noopener">eqanun.ai</a
        >, a legal AI assistant for Azerbaijani law: hybrid dense and lexical retrieval,
        cross-encoder reranking, OCR pipelines for scanned legislation, and the Docker/Kubernetes
        plumbing that keeps it all serving.
      </p>

      <p>
        Working on a low-resource language teaches you things that a benchmark leaderboard never
        will. There is no off-the-shelf embedding model that understands Azerbaijani legal text.
        There is no clean corpus. Half the source documents are scans of scans, in multi-column
        layouts, with tables that mean something. You end up building most of the stack yourself —
        which is exactly why I enjoyed it.
      </p>

      <p>
        Alongside the engineering I ran a research project under the Head of AI on domain-specific
        embedding and reranking models for legal search. The results shipped into the E-qanun AI
        platform and were written up as a technical paper.
      </p>

      <p>
        In September 2025 I moved to Germany to start an <strong>M.Sc. in Computer Science at the
        University of Bonn</strong>, admitted through a paper-based research contest on large
        language models, with an Erasmus Mundus scholarship behind it. My interests have stayed more
        or less where they were: retrieval, embeddings, and getting NLP to work on languages that
        sit outside the well-resourced centre.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside of work I'm slowly grinding through German (A1 and climbing), and I have a soft spot
        for problems that sit at the edge of two fields — like the quantum-inspired reinforcement
        learning agent I prototyped for financial decision-making.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="skills">
      <div class="section__head">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="skills">Skills</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="skills">
        {
          skills.map((group) => (
            <div class="skills__row">
              <dt class="skills__label">{group.group}</dt>
              <dd class="skills__items">
                <ul class="tags">
                  {group.items.map((item) => (
                    <li class="tag">{item}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="languages">
      <div class="section__head">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="languages">Languages</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="langs">
        {
          languages.map((language) => (
            <li class="langs__item">
              <span class="langs__name">{language.name}</span>
              <span class="langs__level">{language.level}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="awards">
      <div class="section__head">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="awards">Awards & scholarships</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="awards">
        {
          awards.map((award) => (
            <li class="awards__item">
              <Icon name="sparkle" size={16} class="awards__icon" />
              <div>
                <p class="awards__title">
                  {award.title} <span class="awards__year">· {award.year}</span>
                </p>
                {award.detail && <p class="awards__detail">{award.detail}</p>}
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="certs">
      <div class="section__head">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="certs">Certifications</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="certs">
        {certifications.map((certification) => <li>{certification}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <p class="closing">
        The short version lives in my <a class="link-inline" href={profile.resume} target="_blank" rel="noopener">résumé</a>,
        and the long version is on the <a class="link-inline" href="/blog/">blog</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .skills {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .skills__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .skills__label {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }

  .skills__items {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .skills__items ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .langs {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(12rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .langs__item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .langs__level {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .awards {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  .awards__item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  :global(.awards__icon) {
    flex: none;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .awards__title {
    font-weight: 550;
  }

  .awards__year {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .awards__detail {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .certs {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .certs li + li {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }

  .closing {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 35.99rem) {
    .skills__row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
